-- 14.5: an annual payer (nothing more due in the year) with a basic premium of 12,000,000 and
-- riders of 1,000,000.
GIVEN yr IS A NUMBER
      amt IS A NUMBER
      rest IS A NUMBER
      acc IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A premium payment`
`a payment in year` yr `of` amt `, still to fall due` rest `, accumulation so far` acc MEANS
    `A premium payment` WITH
        `contract year`                                                   IS yr
        `amount paid`                                                     IS amt
        `basic premium due`                                               IS 12000000
        `rider premiums due`                                              IS 1000000
        `basic and rider premiums of the contract year still to fall due after this one` IS rest
        `accumulation premiums already received in the contract year`    IS acc
-- (i) and (iv): 20,000,000 pays both and leaves 7,000,000 of accumulation premium.
