-- Article 20: 2% is within the maximum, 2.1% is not.
#ASSERT `20 — a fund management charge of` (2%) `is within its maximum, approved maximum` NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `20 — a fund management charge of` (2.1%) `is within its maximum, approved maximum` NOTHING
#ASSERT `20 — a changed fund management charge may be applied, notified on` (YMD 2023 1 1) `, from` (YMD 2023 1 31)

§§ `Chapter 6 — change, reinstatement, termination`

-- Article 21: issued 1 March 2023, received 15 March 2023: the period runs to 5 April 2023.
GIVEN refused IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A free-look refusal`
`a contract issued 1 March 2023, received 15 March 2023, refused on` refused MEANS
    `A free-look refusal` WITH
        `date the contract was issued`                IS YMD 2023 3 1
        `date the policyholder received the contract` IS YMD 2023 3 15
        `date of the refusal`                         IS refused
        `premiums paid`                               IS 20000000
        `medical examination costs`                   IS 1000000
#ASSERT `21 — the refusal is in time` (`a contract issued 1 March 2023, received 15 March 2023, refused on` (YMD 2023 4 5))
#ASSERT NOT `21 — the refusal is in time` (`a contract issued 1 March 2023, received 15 March 2023, refused on` (YMD 2023 4 6))
#ASSERT `21 — the premiums refunded` (`a contract issued 1 March 2023, received 15 March 2023, refused on` (YMD 2023 4 5)) EQUALS 19000000

-- The free-look right as a trace (days from the start of the period): refused on day 10 and
-- refunded on day 20, fulfilled. With no refusal by day 22 the permission lapses unused, which
-- is no breach.
#TRACE `21 — the free-look right` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the policyholder` DOES `refuse to continue the insurance` AT 10
    PARTY `the Company` DOES `refund the premiums paid, without interest, less medical examination costs` AT 20
#TRACE `21 — the free-look right` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 22)

-- 22.1 and 25.1: account value 50,000,000 less debts of 5,000,000.
#ASSERT `22.1 — the amount paid when an organisation policyholder cannot continue, at` `S after cancer, with debts` EQUALS 45000000
#ASSERT `25.1 — the amount paid on surrender, at` `S after cancer, with debts` EQUALS 45000000
#ASSERT count (`22.3 — the steps open to the Company, the insured no longer residing in Vietnam` TRUE) EQUALS 4

-- Article 23: 1,200,000 of cost of insurance due against 1,000,000 deducted: 200,000 to pay; the
-- other way round, 200,000 back into the account value. A true birth date that made the insured
-- 66 on the effective date: the Company may cancel; refund 20,000,000 less debts 5,000,000,
-- medical 1,000,000, withdrawals 2,000,000 and benefits 0 = 12,000,000.
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      due IS A NUMBER
      ded IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A misstatement of age or sex`
`a misstatement, truly born` dob `, cost due` due `, deducted` ded MEANS
    `A misstatement of age or sex` WITH
        `true date of birth`                             IS dob
        `cost of insurance due on the true age and sex`  IS due
        `cost of insurance deducted`                     IS ded
        `premiums paid`                                  IS 20000000
        `medical examination costs`                      IS 1000000
        `withdrawals from the account value`             IS 2000000
        `benefits already paid`                          IS 0
#ASSERT `23.1 — the shortfall of the cost of insurance the policyholder must pay` (`a misstatement, truly born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, cost due` 1200000 `, deducted` 1000000) EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `23.2 — the amount added to the account value, without interest` (`a misstatement, truly born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, cost due` 1000000 `, deducted` 1200000) EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `23.3 — the Company may cancel the contract for` (`a misstatement, truly born` (YMD 1954 6 15) `, cost due` 1000000 `, deducted` 1000000) `under` `C1`
#ASSERT NOT `23.3 — the Company may cancel the contract for` (`a misstatement, truly born` (YMD 1955 6 15) `, cost due` 1000000 `, deducted` 1000000) `under` `C1`
#ASSERT `23.3 — the refund on cancellation for` (`a misstatement, truly born` (YMD 1954 6 15) `, cost due` 1000000 `, deducted` 1000000) `, at` `S after cancer, with debts` EQUALS 12000000

-- Article 24 and 25.2(d): lapsed 1 May 2023 in contract year 3. A request on 1 May 2025 (24
-- months) is in time and the contract has not yet ended; on 2 May 2025 it is late and the
-- contract has ended.
GIVEN req IS A DATE
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A reinstatement request`
`a reinstatement asked on` req `, overdue paid` paid MEANS
    `A reinstatement request` WITH
        `date the contract lapsed`                              IS YMD 2023 5 1
        `contract year in which it lapsed`                      IS 3
        `date of the written request`                           IS req
        `all overdue basic premiums of the compulsory payment period paid` IS paid
        `basic premium instalments due at reinstatement paid`   IS 1
        `evidence of health given and every insurability condition met` IS TRUE
        `date of the Company's approval`                        IS JUST (req PLUS 10)
        `the policyholder and the insured alive at the approval` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `24 — the policyholder may ask to reinstate, by` (`a reinstatement asked on` (YMD 2025 5 1) `, overdue paid` TRUE) `under` `C1`
#ASSERT NOT `24 — the policyholder may ask to reinstate, by` (`a reinstatement asked on` (YMD 2025 5 2) `, overdue paid` TRUE) `under` `C1`
#ASSERT NOT `24 — the policyholder may ask to reinstate, by` (`a reinstatement asked on` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, overdue paid` FALSE) `under` `C1`
#ASSERT `24 — the day the reinstatement takes effect, by` (`a reinstatement asked on` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, overdue paid` TRUE) `under` `C1` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 5 11)
#ASSERT NOT `25.2(d) — a contract lapsed on` (YMD 2023 5 1) `has ended by lapse on` (YMD 2025 5 1)
#ASSERT `25.2(d) — a contract lapsed on` (YMD 2023 5 1) `has ended by lapse on` (YMD 2025 5 2)
#ASSERT `25.2 — the contract ends automatically on` `the Company approves payment of the disability benefit`

§§ `Chapter 7 — claims`

-- Article 26: Lan takes her share; a beneficiary who died first passes the share to the
-- policyholder, or to the heirs if the policyholder has died.
#ASSERT `26.2 — the payee of the share of` (`A beneficiary` WITH `name` IS "Lan", `designated share` IS 60%, `died before the insured` IS FALSE, `took part in the intentional act` IS FALSE) `on` `a natural death in 2030` EQUALS `the beneficiary named` "Lan"
#ASSERT `26.2 — the payee of the share of` (`A beneficiary` WITH `name` IS "Lan", `designated share` IS 60%, `died before the insured` IS TRUE, `took part in the intentional act` IS FALSE) `on` `a natural death in 2030` EQUALS `the policyholder`
#ASSERT `26.1 — the payee of a claim that is not for a death, the claim being` `a cancer claim` EQUALS `the policyholder`
#ASSERT REFUSED `26.1 — the payee of a claim that is not for a death, the claim being` `a death claim`

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of claim`
      acc IS A BOOLEAN
      made IS A DATE
      extra IS A NUMBER
      docs IS A `The documents submitted`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a claim of kind` k `, accident` acc `, for an event on 10 March 2023, made on` made `, extra days` extra `, documents` docs MEANS
    `A claim` WITH
        `kind`                                                 IS k
        `caused by an accident`                                IS acc
        `date of the insured event`                            IS YMD 2023 3 10
        `date the claim was made`                              IS made
        `days spent supplying documents under 27.3 and 27.4`   IS extra
        `the documents`                                        IS docs
        `date the complete and valid file was received`        IS JUST (YMD 2023 6 1)

GIVEN form IS A BOOLEAN
      death IS A BOOLEAN
      accdocs IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The documents submitted`
`documents: form` form `, death extract` death `, accident records` accdocs MEANS
    `The documents submitted` WITH
        `claim form completed fully and accurately`                      IS form
        `extract of the death record`                                    IS death
        `certificate of the injury rate from the medical assessment council or an approved foreign medical organisation` IS FALSE
        `medical evidence from the examining, diagnosing or treating doctor` IS TRUE
        `accident record, scene examination record, forensic and investigation conclusions certified by the competent authority` IS accdocs
        `proof of the right to the benefit, such as a will, and identity papers of the person entitled` IS TRUE
        `proof of the right to receive the benefit, such as an authorisation` IS TRUE

`full death documents` MEANS `documents: form` TRUE `, death extract` TRUE `, accident records` TRUE
#ASSERT `27 — the documents are complete for` (`a claim of kind` `a death claim` `, accident` TRUE `, for an event on 10 March 2023, made on` (YMD 2023 4 1) `, extra days` 0 `, documents` `full death documents`)
#ASSERT NOT `27 — the documents are complete for` (`a claim of kind` `a death claim` `, accident` TRUE `, for an event on 10 March 2023, made on` (YMD 2023 4 1) `, extra days` 0 `, documents` (`documents: form` TRUE `, death extract` TRUE `, accident records` FALSE))
#ASSERT `27 — the documents are complete for` (`a claim of kind` `a death claim` `, accident` FALSE `, for an event on 10 March 2023, made on` (YMD 2023 4 1) `, extra days` 0 `, documents` (`documents: form` TRUE `, death extract` TRUE `, accident records` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `27 — the documents are complete for` (`a claim of kind` `a disability claim` `, accident` FALSE `, for an event on 10 March 2023, made on` (YMD 2023 4 1) `, extra days` 0 `, documents` `full death documents`)
#ASSERT `27 — the documents are complete for` (`a claim of kind` `a maturity claim` `, accident` FALSE `, for an event on 10 March 2023, made on` (YMD 2023 4 1) `, extra days` 0 `, documents` (`documents: form` TRUE `, death extract` FALSE `, accident records` FALSE))

